1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,921
What if one day your body can no longer take you where you want to go?\N{\fs18}如果有一天，你的身體無法再帶你去想去的地方？

2
00:00:04,908 --> 00:00:08,005
What if you wake up and there is nowhere you want to go anyway?\N{\fs18}如果你醒來，發現根本沒有想去的地方？

3
00:00:08,985 --> 00:00:13,147
And when so much of the person you used to be is gone, what is still there?\N{\fs18}當當年的你已逝去大半，還剩下什麼？

4
00:00:18,836 --> 00:00:20,541
When I think about growing old,\N{\fs18}想到變老，

5
00:00:20,810 --> 00:00:22,785
I don't have to imagine very much.\N{\fs18}我不用費力想像。

6
00:00:23,772 --> 00:00:25,860
My grandmother had a stroke and spent\N{\fs18}我祖母中風，

7
00:00:25,874 --> 00:00:28,076
more than ten years in a nursing home.\N{\fs18}在養護院度過了十多年。

8
00:00:29,056 --> 00:00:30,817
She lost the ability to speak,\N{\fs18}她失去了說話的能力，

9
00:00:31,073 --> 00:00:32,295
and much of her ability\N{\fs18}也失去了大部分

10
00:00:32,309 --> 00:00:33,658
to communicate with us.\N{\fs18}與我們溝通的能力。

11
00:00:34,638 --> 00:00:36,243
After my father retired,\N{\fs18}父親退休後，

12
00:00:36,499 --> 00:00:38,630
his world gradually became smaller.\N{\fs18}他的世界逐漸縮小。

13
00:00:39,610 --> 00:00:42,706
He spent most of his time at home watching television.\N{\fs18}他大多數時間待在家看電視。

14
00:00:43,687 --> 00:00:47,053
Health problems eventually made even going out difficult.\N{\fs18}健康問題最後連出門都變得困難。

15
00:00:48,033 --> 00:00:51,655
My mother began showing signs of dementia after an accident.\N{\fs18}母親在一次意外後開始出現失智徵兆。

16
00:00:52,635 --> 00:00:55,547
On days when she doesn't go to a day care center,\N{\fs18}不去日照中心的日子，

17
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,246
she can spend hours simply sitting in a chair.\N{\fs18}她能坐在椅子上坐上好幾個鐘頭。

18
00:00:59,948 --> 00:01:00,942
When I look at them,\N{\fs18}看著他們，

19
00:01:01,155 --> 00:01:03,045
my first reaction is simple:\N{\fs18}我的第一反應很單純：

20
00:01:04,032 --> 00:01:05,779
I don't want to grow old like that.\N{\fs18}我不想以那種方式變老。

21
00:01:06,759 --> 00:01:09,216
But then comes a more uncomfortable thought.\N{\fs18}但緊接著浮現一個更讓人不安的念頭。

22
00:01:10,196 --> 00:01:11,915
What if I don't get to choose?\N{\fs18}如果我沒得選擇呢？

23
00:01:13,604 --> 00:01:14,783
I can exercise,\N{\fs18}我可以運動，

24
00:01:14,953 --> 00:01:15,948
watch what I eat,\N{\fs18}注意飲食，

25
00:01:16,189 --> 00:01:17,027
and save enough\N{\fs18}存夠錢

26
00:01:17,042 --> 00:01:18,348
money for retirement.\N{\fs18}準備退休。

27
00:01:19,335 --> 00:01:20,315
But none of these can\N{\fs18}但這些都無法保證

28
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:21,821
guarantee what kind of old\N{\fs18}我會變成什麼樣的

29
00:01:21,835 --> 00:01:23,185
person I will become.\N{\fs18}老人。

30
00:01:24,165 --> 00:01:26,210
I may lose the ability to travel.\N{\fs18}我可能失去旅行的能力。

31
00:01:27,190 --> 00:01:30,017
I may need help getting through an ordinary day.\N{\fs18}我可能需要幫助才能過完平凡的一天。

32
00:01:30,997 --> 00:01:33,455
I may no longer be able to read for hours\N{\fs18}我可能再也無法連續閱讀好幾個鐘頭

33
00:01:33,469 --> 00:01:35,855
or sit in front of a laptop working on some\N{\fs18}或坐在筆電前

34
00:01:35,869 --> 00:01:38,057
project that nobody asked me to do.\N{\fs18}做著沒人要求的專案。

35
00:01:39,037 --> 00:01:40,358
All of that scares me.\N{\fs18}這一切都讓我害怕。

36
00:01:42,044 --> 00:01:44,601
But what scares me most is something simpler:\N{\fs18}但最讓我害怕的，其實更單純：

37
00:01:45,588 --> 00:01:48,656
Waking up in the morning and having nothing I want to do.\N{\fs18}早上醒來，發現沒有任何想做的事。

38
00:01:50,348 --> 00:01:53,885
Right now, there are always things I want to experience,\N{\fs18}現在總有想體驗、

39
00:01:54,084 --> 00:01:56,768
understand, make, or write down.\N{\fs18}想理解、想創作、想記錄的事。

40
00:01:57,755 --> 00:01:59,886
I want to go somewhere I haven't been,\N{\fs18}想去從未去過的地方，

41
00:02:00,142 --> 00:02:01,477
see how people live there,\N{\fs18}看看那裡的人怎麼生活，

42
00:02:01,761 --> 00:02:02,585
then come back,\N{\fs18}然後回來，

43
00:02:02,883 --> 00:02:03,963
open my laptop,\N{\fs18}打開筆電，

44
00:02:04,204 --> 00:02:05,042
and work on one\N{\fs18}繼續做

45
00:02:05,057 --> 00:02:06,164
of my projects.\N{\fs18}我的專案。

46
00:02:07,145 --> 00:02:08,395
Something comes in.\N{\fs18}總有東西進來。

47
00:02:09,375 --> 00:02:10,156
And I still have\N{\fs18}我還有

48
00:02:10,170 --> 00:02:10,937
something I want\N{\fs18}想送出去的

49
00:02:10,951 --> 00:02:12,173
to send back out.\N{\fs18}東西。

50
00:02:13,868 --> 00:02:17,348
Maybe this is one thing we underestimate about retirement.\N{\fs18}也許這是我們低估退休生活的一環。

51
00:02:18,335 --> 00:02:19,926
Work gives us more than money.\N{\fs18}工作給我們的不只金錢。

52
00:02:20,906 --> 00:02:22,057
It gives us structure,\N{\fs18}它給我們結構、

53
00:02:22,241 --> 00:02:23,434
problems to solve,\N{\fs18}待解的問題、

54
00:02:23,662 --> 00:02:24,656
people to talk to,\N{\fs18}可聊的人、

55
00:02:24,883 --> 00:02:25,778
and things that have\N{\fs18}非做完

56
00:02:25,792 --> 00:02:26,645
to be finished.\N{\fs18}不可的事。

57
00:02:27,625 --> 00:02:29,670
Then one day, it stops.\N{\fs18}然後有一天，它停了。

58
00:02:31,364 --> 00:02:34,034
I can tell myself I will have plenty to do.\N{\fs18}我可以告訴自己會有很多事可做。

59
00:02:35,021 --> 00:02:36,982
I already have too many projects\N{\fs18}我已經有太多專案、

60
00:02:36,996 --> 00:02:39,198
and too many places I want to see.\N{\fs18}太多想去的地方。

61
00:02:40,178 --> 00:02:42,663
But what will I want when I am seventy-five?\N{\fs18}但七十五歲時，我會想要什麼？

62
00:02:43,644 --> 00:02:44,752
I don't really know.\N{\fs18}我真的不知道。

63
00:02:46,436 --> 00:02:49,149
There is another part of growing old that bothers me.\N{\fs18}變老還有另一件讓我介意的事。

64
00:02:50,136 --> 00:02:51,770
I don't want to become a burden.\N{\fs18}我不想成為負擔。

65
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:54,795
I want my child to care about me.\N{\fs18}我希望孩子在乎我。

66
00:02:55,775 --> 00:02:57,551
But I don't want his life to revolve\N{\fs18}但不想他的人生

67
00:02:57,565 --> 00:02:59,127
around taking care of me.\N{\fs18}圍繞著照顧我轉。

68
00:03:00,108 --> 00:03:02,224
I don't need complete independence.\N{\fs18}我不需要完全獨立。

69
00:03:03,204 --> 00:03:04,610
Some help is fine.\N{\fs18}接受幫助沒關係。

70
00:03:05,591 --> 00:03:06,571
What bothers me is\N{\fs18}介意的

71
00:03:06,585 --> 00:03:07,480
the thought of another\N{\fs18}是，另一個

72
00:03:07,494 --> 00:03:08,588
person's life being\N{\fs18}人的生命被

73
00:03:08,602 --> 00:03:10,363
consumed by my needs.\N{\fs18}我的需求吞噬。

74
00:03:12,068 --> 00:03:13,261
And, to be honest,\N{\fs18}誠實說，

75
00:03:13,559 --> 00:03:14,639
I am really hoping\N{\fs18}我真希望

76
00:03:14,653 --> 00:03:15,363
we will have good\N{\fs18}那時候有好的

77
00:03:15,378 --> 00:03:16,940
care robots by then.\N{\fs18}照護機器人。

78
00:03:17,927 --> 00:03:19,348
If technology and a good\N{\fs18}如果科技和

79
00:03:19,362 --> 00:03:20,967
care system can handle more\N{\fs18}照護體系能分擔更多

80
00:03:20,981 --> 00:03:22,160
of the day-to-day care,\N{\fs18}日常照護，

81
00:03:22,430 --> 00:03:23,865
perhaps my family doesn't\N{\fs18}或許家人

82
00:03:23,879 --> 00:03:25,683
have to become my care system.\N{\fs18}就不用變成我的照護系統。

83
00:03:26,663 --> 00:03:28,637
They can simply remain my family.\N{\fs18}他們可以單純地只是我的家人。

84
00:03:30,332 --> 00:03:32,960
So imagine an ordinary Tuesday morning.\N{\fs18}想像一個普通的週二早晨。

85
00:03:33,947 --> 00:03:35,523
I am eighty years old.\N{\fs18}我八十歲了。

86
00:03:36,504 --> 00:03:38,379
There is nowhere I have to be.\N{\fs18}不用去任何地方。

87
00:03:39,359 --> 00:03:41,475
Nobody is waiting for my work.\N{\fs18}沒人等我的工作。

88
00:03:42,455 --> 00:03:44,387
My child has his own life.\N{\fs18}孩子有他自己的生活。

89
00:03:45,371 --> 00:03:46,294
What would make me want\N{\fs18}什麼會讓我

90
00:03:46,308 --> 00:03:47,444
to get out of bed?\N{\fs18}想起床？

91
00:03:49,124 --> 00:03:50,985
I think I would still like to ask:\N{\fs18}我想我仍會想問：

92
00:03:51,972 --> 00:03:53,804
How can I live this day well?\N{\fs18}如何好好過這一天？

93
00:03:54,784 --> 00:03:55,977
And is there something I can\N{\fs18}我能在世界上

94
00:03:55,992 --> 00:03:57,469
leave behind in the world?\N{\fs18}留下點什麼嗎？

95
00:03:58,449 --> 00:04:00,097
I don't mean anything grand.\N{\fs18}不指什麼大事。

96
00:04:01,077 --> 00:04:02,526
Maybe a few strangers\N{\fs18}也許幾個陌生人

97
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:03,847
read something I wrote,\N{\fs18}讀了我寫的東西，

98
00:04:04,017 --> 00:04:05,296
watch a video I made,\N{\fs18}看了我做的影片，

99
00:04:05,523 --> 00:04:06,517
or use some little\N{\fs18}用了我做的

100
00:04:06,531 --> 00:04:07,710
project I built.\N{\fs18}小專案。

101
00:04:08,690 --> 00:04:10,225
People I will never meet.\N{\fs18}這些人我此生不會見面。

102
00:04:11,824 --> 00:04:13,396
For most of my life,\N{\fs18}人生大半，

103
00:04:13,397 --> 00:04:15,441
the world has been sending\N{\fs18}世界都在向我輸入

104
00:04:15,442 --> 00:04:17,722
things into me—books, places,\N{\fs18}書籍、地方、

105
00:04:17,723 --> 00:04:20,160
people, questions, experiences.\N{\fs18}人、問題、經驗。

106
00:04:20,161 --> 00:04:22,048
I hope I will still have\N{\fs18}我希望仍能

107
00:04:22,049 --> 00:04:23,857
something to send back.\N{\fs18}輸出點什麼。

108
00:04:23,858 --> 00:04:25,981
Not because I need to prove\N{\fs18}不是為了證明

109
00:04:25,982 --> 00:04:27,318
that I am useful.\N{\fs18}我有用。

110
00:04:27,319 --> 00:04:30,464
Just because the conversation between me\N{\fs18}只因為我與世界的

111
00:04:30,465 --> 00:04:32,982
and the world is still going on.\N{\fs18}對話還在繼續。

112
00:04:34,676 --> 00:04:38,057
But even that may be asking too much of my future self.\N{\fs18}但即使這樣，或許也對未來的我要求太高。

113
00:04:39,044 --> 00:04:43,177
Maybe one day I won't be able to write or work on projects anymore.\N{\fs18}或許有一天我寫不了字、做不了專案。

114
00:04:44,157 --> 00:04:47,595
Maybe I will just sit by a window, listen to music,\N{\fs18}也許我就坐在窗邊，聽聽音樂，

115
00:04:47,865 --> 00:04:49,569
eat something I still enjoy,\N{\fs18}吃點仍覺得好吃的東西，

116
00:04:49,796 --> 00:04:51,870
and talk to someone once in a while.\N{\fs18}偶爾跟人說說話。

117
00:04:52,850 --> 00:04:54,725
If I am not in constant pain,\N{\fs18}若無長期疼痛，

118
00:04:54,939 --> 00:04:55,862
perhaps that would be\N{\fs18}或許那也是

119
00:04:55,876 --> 00:04:57,240
a pretty good day too.\N{\fs18}不錯的一天。

120
00:04:58,940 --> 00:05:02,449
It would be easy to turn aging into another performance target:\N{\fs18}很容易把變老變成另一項績效指標：

121
00:05:02,662 --> 00:05:04,778
stay curious, stay productive,\N{\fs18}保持好奇、保持產出、

122
00:05:05,062 --> 00:05:07,122
remain useful until the very end.\N{\fs18}到最後一刻仍有用。

123
00:05:08,109 --> 00:05:10,907
Maybe growing old gracefully also means knowing\N{\fs18}也許體面地老去，

124
00:05:10,921 --> 00:05:13,791
when I no longer have to prove any of those things.\N{\fs18}就是知道何時不必再證明那些事。

125
00:05:15,476 --> 00:05:20,540
And perhaps there is one more thing I hope I can let go of. Regret.\N{\fs18}或許還有一件事，我希望能放下後悔。

126
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:27,102
My eighty-year-old self may look back at me today and say: You had enough money.\N{\fs18}八十歲的我可能回頭看現在的我說：你錢夠了。

127
00:05:28,082 --> 00:05:31,548
Why didn't you stop working earlier and do what you really wanted?\N{\fs18}為何不早點停下來，做真正想做的事？

128
00:05:32,528 --> 00:05:35,753
Or he may say: You needed the money.\N{\fs18}或者他會說：你需要錢。

129
00:05:36,733 --> 00:05:38,721
Why didn't you work a few more years\N{\fs18}為何趁還能工作時

130
00:05:38,736 --> 00:05:39,858
while you still could?\N{\fs18}不多幹幾年？

131
00:05:41,540 --> 00:05:42,037
I don't know\N{\fs18}我不知道

132
00:05:42,051 --> 00:05:42,790
which old man\N{\fs18}我會變成

133
00:05:42,804 --> 00:05:43,628
I will become.\N{\fs18}哪種老人。

134
00:05:44,615 --> 00:05:45,993
I have to make decisions\N{\fs18}我得

135
00:05:46,007 --> 00:05:47,186
now without knowing how\N{\fs18}在不知結局時

136
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:48,649
the story turns out.\N{\fs18}做決定。

137
00:05:49,629 --> 00:05:50,766
Maybe that is what\N{\fs18}也許這就是

138
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:52,442
makes regret so unfair.\N{\fs18}後悔最不公平的地方。

139
00:05:53,422 --> 00:05:54,984
We judge our younger selves\N{\fs18}我們用年輕的自己

140
00:05:54,999 --> 00:05:56,774
with information they never had.\N{\fs18}從未擁有的資訊，來審判他們。

141
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:01,684
So perhaps growing old gracefully is not reaching the end\N{\fs18}也許體面地老去，

142
00:06:01,699 --> 00:06:04,383
and discovering that I made all the right choices.\N{\fs18}不是走到終點發現全對了。

143
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:07,274
Perhaps it is being able to look back\N{\fs18}而是能回頭

144
00:06:07,288 --> 00:06:09,305
at the person I used to be and say:\N{\fs18}看著過去的自己說：

145
00:06:10,285 --> 00:06:11,691
You made the best choices you\N{\fs18}你用當時擁有的認知，

146
00:06:11,705 --> 00:06:13,197
could with what you knew then.\N{\fs18}做了最好的選擇。

147
00:06:14,177 --> 00:06:15,441
Don't spend what's left\N{\fs18}別把剩下的時間

148
00:06:15,455 --> 00:06:17,231
regretting the choices you made.\N{\fs18}花在後悔那些選擇上。

149
00:06:18,211 --> 00:06:20,058
There isn't that much road ahead.\N{\fs18}前路不長了。

150
00:06:21,038 --> 00:06:23,069
Just live the last part of the journey.\N{\fs18}就好好走完旅程的最後一程。
